    description: "SCIP's DescriptorKind.METHOD covers a Rust FREE FUNCTION as well as a method:\n`load_config().` parses as METHOD because of the `(...)` disambiguator, so\nscip/index.py maps both onto Symbol.kind=\"method\". Measured on aardvark-dns at\nb1008d3b67: all 52 free functions emitted by both arms are `method` per SCIP\nand `function` per tree-sitter. The descriptor CHAIN carries the answer (a\nparent TYPE descriptor means method; a parent NAMESPACE means free function)\nand the importer does not consult it. Recorded first on WI-gojum 2026-09-17.\n\nWHY IT MATTERS NOW (ADR-0057): `kind` becomes a contested attribute on every\nmerged record. Arbitration only helps when at least one side is right; today\nthe type-aware backend is the WRONG one on this attribute, which is why\nADR-0057 refuses \"type-aware wins\" as the built-in default. Fixing the\nproducer removes the contest on 52/52 instead of arbitrating it.\n\nFIX SHAPE: in index.py `_name_and_kind`, walk parse_scip_symbol's descriptor\nlist; METHOD whose immediate parent is TYPE -> \"method\", whose parent is\nNAMESPACE (or none) -> \"function\". Values must exist in the symbol-kind\nregistry (ADR-0027).\n\nACCEPTANCE: the 52 pairs agree on kind; the 27 true methods still say method."  # 85e2
    fields: {}  # 85e2
- op: discuss  # a895
  at: '2026-09-18T20:43:21Z'  # a895
  by: agent  # a895
  actor: jgstern_agent  # a895
  clock: 2  # a895
  nonce: a895  # a895
  message: "WIDENED 2026-09-18 (owner: \"agreed\"). Not only free functions. On the same\naardvark-dns artifact, 9 of 9 enum VARIANTS pair SCIP kind=class against\ntree-sitter kind=field: rust-analyzer emits a variant as a Type descriptor\n(`SubCommand#Run#`), index.py maps `#` -> class, tree-sitter emits the\nvariant as field. So the descriptor-chain rule must also read: a Type\ndescriptor whose PARENT is a Type is a variant (or nested type), not a\nclass. Acceptance widens: 52/52 free functions agree on kind AND 9/9\nvariants agree; the 27 true methods and the 10 structs are unchanged.\nWhether the variant lands as `field` (tree-sitter's choice) or a\nregistered variant kind is an ADR-0027 symbol-kind question — check the\nregistry before choosing; do not mint a new kind here."  # a895
